---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Create a board or a folder with this name.
It prints the new node with its link.

USAGE
  holst board create <name> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  name   The name of the new board or folder

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws    The workspace a new thing goes to: id or part of its name; needed when you have several
      --folder folder   The folder it goes into: a folder id, link or part of its name; / is the root; the workspace root by default
  -k, --kind kind       What to create: board or folder; board by default
  -n, --dry-run         Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b create "Roadmap" -w easy
  $ holst b create "Plans" -k folder -w easy

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
